# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the Python version is generally
#   managed by the user. However, for a specific project, it's fine to include them.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if you want to keep the local dependencies separately,
#   you can add Pipfile.lock here.
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include poetry.lock in version control.
#   poetry.lock
#   pyproject.toml is usually tracked.

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include pdm.lock in version control.
# pdm.lock
# .pdm-python
# .pdm-build/

